  "methodLimits": [
    "Sequential A/B/A, with one candidate window and two corrected-control windows. The return to control was added to check the observed CPU increase; this is not a randomized statistical benchmark.",
    "The same VM stays running across all three windows; reconnecting each viewer resets decoder/server stream state. Steady windows have zero additional stream-create messages. Counts at window start differ because of reconnection activity.",
    "Actual Display observation windows and CPU intervals differ; rates use their own recorded timestamps. CPU uses same-host monotonic intervals, never cross-host clock subtraction.",
    "AX counters are periodically sampled and best effort across actors; native/decoded is an approximate composition ratio, not exact per-fragment rejection attribution.",
    "Timing p95/max values are cumulative session histograms; no percentile or maximum subtraction is performed. Framed-receive idle gaps include deliberate pauses between test actions.",
    "The source requests 30 FPS with a finite 5400-callback timer. Its scheduling and the QEMU capture cadence are not verified output FPS; automatic server bitrate/quality and fragment arrival rate can vary.",
    "GPU bytes count canonical copy work, not measured hardware bandwidth utilization. Copy waits include GPU queue/completion and actor resumption.",
    "Native commits and stream messages count fragments. Metal presentations can repeat a partially updated Surface; no complete-frame FPS or per-key photon latency is inferred.",
    "Screenshot color phases are unaligned; visible band reduction is qualitative. No pixel-quality score or source-frame age is established.",
    "Pool exhaustion and readbacks are lifetime/delta diagnostics; they are retained as remaining resource pressure, not silently discarded.",
    "The CPU fallback field in Native / CPU fallback / Metal disabled counts advanced-video fallback. MJPEG Data fallback counts decoder output storage, not all possible composition fallbacks. The native-video fallback counter was not captured in AX; the residual decoded-minus-native gap remains unclassified.",
    "Process memory endpoints are gauges after different warmups and do not establish a peak-memory improvement."
  ],
